# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""R3 node definitions (hand-specified judgement; numbers cite lab files).
Fields: id, theme, label, P/Ps (professor claim-matrix propositions: primary/secondary), X/Xs (executive), pitems/eitems (chair items),
ps/es (panel strength), data, dfiles, crule (class by the mechanical rule), ruling, cls (final class after coordinator rulings),
dest (destination), dec (decision), key (key numbers: market, period, gross/net), settle (settling test / data need, for non-core nodes).
Panel strength rubric: Strong = chair consensus/refutation held by >=3 members with checks MATCH/CONFIRMED; Moderate = consensus held by 1-2
members, QUALIFIED checks, or reached after cross-examination/concession; Weak = minority, single unverified claim or backlog-level endorsement;
Split = chair lists it as contested inside the panel; Silent = no ledger claim and no chair item; Refuted = the panel refutes/withdraws it.
"""
